  "AGENTS.md": "# my-app

Stack: Astro, TypeScript, Sass, Tailwind CSS, Axios, Playwright, Vitest, ESLint, Prettier, Husky, lint-staged, SEO, llms.txt, GitHub Actions.

## Commands

- \`npm install\`: install dependencies
- \`npm run dev\`: start the dev server
- \`npm run build\`: production build
- \`npm run preview\`: serve the production build
- \`npm run astro\`
- \`npm run typecheck\`: type-check
- \`npm run test:e2e\`
- \`npm run test\`: run the tests once
- \`npm run lint\`: lint
- \`npm run format\`: format all files
- \`npm run format:check\`: check formatting
- \`npm run deploy\`: build and publish the site (ask first)

## Project structure

- Pages are \`.astro\` files in \`src/pages/\`; layouts in \`src/layouts/\`, components in \`src/components/\`.

## Conventions

- Pages render to static HTML; interactivity goes in \`<script>\` tags or client islands.
- Style with Tailwind CSS utility classes (v4: configuration lives in CSS, there is no tailwind.config).
- Global styles are SCSS.
- Call the API through the shared Axios client; its base URL comes from an environment variable (see \`.env.example\`).
- Tests use Vitest; put \`*.test.*\` files next to the code they test.
- ESLint flat config in \`eslint.config.*\`; fix lint errors instead of disabling rules.
- Prettier formats the code; don't hand-format.
- SEO metadata, sitemap and robots.txt are generated from the site URL; keep page titles and descriptions meaningful.
- TypeScript strict mode; avoid \`any\`.

## Before finishing a change

Run \`npm run lint\`, \`npm run typecheck\`, \`npm run test\` and fix what they report.
",
  "CLAUDE.md": "@AGENTS.md

## Claude Code

- After a change, run \`npm run lint\`, \`npm run typecheck\`, \`npm run test\` before reporting it done.
- Edited files are formatted automatically by a hook; don't reformat by hand.
- MCP servers for this stack are in \`.mcp.json\` (astro-docs); prefer them over guessing APIs.
- Keep secrets in \`.env.local\`; Claude is not allowed to read \`.env\` files.
",
  "Dockerfile": "# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1

FROM node:24-alpine AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json package-lock.json* ./
RUN npm install
COPY . .
RUN npm run build

FROM nginx:1.29-alpine
COPY nginx.conf /etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf
COPY --from=build /app/dist /usr/share/nginx/html
EXPOSE 80
