  "README.md" => "# my-app

Stack: Next.js (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, PostgreSQL, Drizzle ORM.

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
npm install
npm run dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`npm run build\`
- \`npm run start\`
- \`npm run typecheck\`
- \`npm run db:push\`
- \`npm run db:generate\`
- \`npm run db:migrate\`
- \`npm run db:studio\`

## Database

Start PostgreSQL (needs Docker), copy \`.env.example\` to \`.env\`, then create the tables from \`db/schema.ts\`:

\`\`\`bash
docker compose up -d
npm run db:push
\`\`\`

\`/todos\` lists and adds rows. Use \`npm run db:generate\` and \`npm run db:migrate\` for versioned migrations, and \`npm run db:studio\` to browse the data.

## Push to GitHub

Create an empty repository on GitHub, then:

\`\`\`bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/my-app.git
git push -u origin main
\`\`\`
