  "AGENTS.md": "# my-app

Stack: Next.js (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Sass, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Redux Toolkit, Axios, Playwright, Vitest, Testing Library, ESLint, Prettier, Husky, lint-staged, SEO, llms.txt, GitHub Actions.

## Commands

- \`npm install\`: install dependencies
- \`npm run dev\`: start the dev server
- \`npm run build\`: production build
- \`npm run start\`: serve the production build
- \`npm run typecheck\`: type-check
- \`npm run test:e2e\`
- \`npm run test\`: run the tests once
- \`npm run lint\`: lint
- \`npm run format\`: format all files
- \`npm run format:check\`: check formatting

## Project structure

- App Router: routes are folders in \`app/\` with \`page\` and \`layout\` files; components in \`components/\`.
- \`@/\` points to the project root.

## Conventions

- Components are Server Components by default; add \`"use client"\` only where state, effects or event handlers are needed.
- Set page titles through the \`metadata\` export, not \`<head>\` tags.
- Style with Tailwind CSS utility classes (v4: configuration lives in CSS, there is no tailwind.config).
- Global styles are SCSS.
- UI components come from shadcn/ui in \`components/ui\`; add new ones with \`npx shadcn@latest add <component>\` rather than writing them by hand.
- Shared state lives in the Redux Toolkit store; add state as slices.
- Call the API through the shared Axios client; its base URL comes from an environment variable (see \`.env.example\`).
- Tests use Vitest; put \`*.test.*\` files next to the code they test.
- Component tests use Testing Library: query by role or text and simulate users with \`user-event\`.
- ESLint flat config in \`eslint.config.*\`; fix lint errors instead of disabling rules.
- Prettier formats the code; don't hand-format.
- SEO metadata, sitemap and robots.txt are generated from the site URL; keep page titles and descriptions meaningful.
- TypeScript strict mode; avoid \`any\`.

## Before finishing a change

Run \`npm run lint\`, \`npm run typecheck\`, \`npm run test\` and fix what they report.
",
  "CLAUDE.md": "@AGENTS.md

## Claude Code

- After a change, run \`npm run lint\`, \`npm run typecheck\`, \`npm run test\` before reporting it done.
- Edited files are formatted automatically by a hook; don't reformat by hand.
- MCP servers for this stack are in \`.mcp.json\` (next-devtools, shadcn); prefer them over guessing APIs.
- Keep secrets in \`.env.local\`; Claude is not allowed to read \`.env\` files.
",
  "Dockerfile": "# syntax=docker/dockerfile:1

FROM node:24-alpine AS build
WORKDIR /app
COPY package.json package-lock.json* ./
RUN npm install
COPY . .
RUN mkdir -p public
RUN npm run build

FROM node:24-alpine
WORKDIR /app
ENV NODE_ENV=production
ENV PORT=3000
ENV HOSTNAME=0.0.0.0
COPY --from=build --chown=node:node /app/public ./public
COPY --from=build --chown=node:node /app/.next/standalone ./
COPY --from=build --chown=node:node /app/.next/static ./.next/static
USER node
EXPOSE 3000
CMD ["node", "server.js"]
