  "README.md": "# my-app

Stack: Next.js (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, Sass, Tailwind CSS, shadcn/ui, Redux Toolkit, Axios, Playwright, Vitest, Testing Library, ESLint, Prettier, Husky, lint-staged, SEO, llms.txt, GitHub Actions.

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
npm install
npm run dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`npm run build\`
- \`npm run start\`
- \`npm run typecheck\`
- \`npm run test:e2e\`
- \`npm run test\`
- \`npm run lint\`
- \`npm run format\`
- \`npm run format:check\`
- \`npm run prepare\`

## UI components

shadcn/ui components live in \`components/ui\`. Add more with \`npx shadcn@latest add <component>\`.

## API client

Copy \`.env.example\` to \`.env\` and set \`NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL\`. Import the client from \`api/client\`.

## End-to-end tests

Install the browser once, then run the tests (they start the dev server themselves):

\`\`\`sh
npx playwright install chromium
npm run test:e2e
\`\`\`

## Git hooks

The pre-commit hook runs lint-staged on staged files (lint-staged needs Node.js 22.22.1 or newer). Hooks are installed by \`prepare\` during install, which needs a git repository: after \`git init\`, run the install once more.

## License

MIT, see \`LICENSE\`.

## Docker

\`\`\`sh
docker build -t my-app .
docker run --rm -p 3000:3000 my-app
\`\`\`

Then open http://localhost:3000.

## Deploy to Netlify

Push the project to GitHub and import it at https://app.netlify.com/start.
Netlify detects the framework and sets up its server runtime; no config file is needed.

Or deploy from the terminal with \`npx netlify-cli deploy\`.

## Deploy to Vercel

Push the project to GitHub and import it at https://vercel.com/new. Vercel detects Next.js and needs no build settings.

Or deploy from the terminal with \`npx vercel\`.

## Claude Code

\`CLAUDE.md\` (with \`AGENTS.md\`) describes the project, \`.claude/settings.json\` allows the project's scripts and formats edited files, and \`.mcp.json\` lists MCP servers for the stack (Claude Code asks before enabling them).

## SEO

Set \`NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL\` to your public origin (defaults to \`https://example.com\`). It is used for canonical URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt and llms.txt.

## Push to GitHub

Create an empty repository on GitHub, then:

\`\`\`bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/my-app.git
git push -u origin main
\`\`\`
",
  "api/client.ts": "import axios from "axios";

export const api = axios.create({
  baseURL: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL ?? "http://localhost:3000",
  timeout: 10_000,
});
