  "README.md": "# my-app

Stack: Nuxt 4, Vue 3, TypeScript, Sass, Tailwind CSS, shadcn-vue, Pinia, Axios, Playwright, Vitest, Testing Library, ESLint, Prettier, Husky, lint-staged, SEO, llms.txt, GitHub Actions.

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
npm install
npm run dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`npm run build\`
- \`npm run generate\`
- \`npm run preview\`
- \`npm run postinstall\`
- \`npm run typecheck\`
- \`npm run test:e2e\`
- \`npm run test\`
- \`npm run lint\`
- \`npm run format\`
- \`npm run format:check\`
- \`npm run prepare\`

## UI components

shadcn-vue components live in \`app/components/ui\`. Add more with \`npx shadcn-vue@latest add <component>\`.

## API client

Set \`NUXT_PUBLIC_API_URL\` (see \`.env.example\`). Use the client via \`const { $api } = useNuxtApp()\`.

## End-to-end tests

Install the browser once, then run the tests (they start the dev server themselves):

\`\`\`sh
npx playwright install chromium
npm run test:e2e
\`\`\`

## Git hooks

The pre-commit hook runs lint-staged on staged files (lint-staged needs Node.js 22.22.1 or newer). Hooks are installed by \`prepare\` during install, which needs a git repository: after \`git init\`, run the install once more.

## License

MIT, see \`LICENSE\`.

## Docker

\`\`\`sh
docker build -t my-app .
docker run --rm -p 3000:3000 my-app
\`\`\`

Then open http://localhost:3000.

## Deploy to Netlify

Push the project to GitHub and import it at https://app.netlify.com/start.
Netlify detects the framework and sets up its server runtime; no config file is needed.

Or deploy from the terminal with \`npx netlify-cli deploy\`.

## Deploy to Vercel

Push the project to GitHub and import it at https://vercel.com/new. Vercel detects Nuxt and needs no build settings.

Or deploy from the terminal with \`npx vercel\`.

## Claude Code

\`CLAUDE.md\` (with \`AGENTS.md\`) describes the project, \`.claude/settings.json\` allows the project's scripts and formats edited files, and \`.mcp.json\` lists MCP servers for the stack (Claude Code asks before enabling them).

## SEO

Set \`NUXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL\` to your public origin (defaults to \`https://example.com\`). It is used for canonical URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt and llms.txt.

## Push to GitHub

Create an empty repository on GitHub, then:

\`\`\`bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/my-app.git
git push -u origin main
\`\`\`
",
  "app/app.vue": "<script setup lang="ts">
const { siteUrl } = useRuntimeConfig().public;
const route = useRoute();

useHead({
  link: [{ rel: "canonical", href: () => \`\${siteUrl}\${route.path}\` }],
  script: [
    {
      type: "application/ld+json",
      innerHTML: JSON.stringify({
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "WebSite",
        name: "my-app",
        url: siteUrl,
      }),
    },
  ],
});

useSeoMeta({
  description: "my-app: a web app.",
  ogType: "website",
  ogSiteName: "my-app",
  ogUrl: () => \`\${siteUrl}\${route.path}\`,
  twitterCard: "summary",
});
</script>

<template>
  <NuxtRouteAnnouncer />
  <main
    class="flex min-h-screen flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 bg-slate-50 p-8 text-slate-900"
  >
    <nav class="flex gap-4 text-sm font-medium">
      <NuxtLink class="text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900" to="/">
        Home
      </NuxtLink>
      <NuxtLink class="text-slate-600 hover:text-slate-900" to="/about">
        About
      </NuxtLink>
    </nav>
    <NuxtPage />
  </main>
</template>
