  "README.md": "# my-app

Stack: SolidJS, Vite, Sass, Tailwind CSS, Solid signals store, Solid Router, Axios, TanStack Query, TanStack Form, Zod, Playwright, Vitest, Testing Library, ESLint, Prettier, Husky, lint-staged, SEO, llms.txt, PWA, GitHub Actions.

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
npm install
npm run dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`npm run build\`
- \`npm run preview\`
- \`npm run test:e2e\`
- \`npm run test\`
- \`npm run lint\`
- \`npm run format\`
- \`npm run format:check\`
- \`npm run prepare\`
- \`npm run deploy\`

## API client

Copy \`.env.example\` to \`.env\` and set \`VITE_API_URL\`. Import the client from \`src/api/client\`.

## End-to-end tests

Install the browser once, then run the tests (they start the dev server themselves):

\`\`\`sh
npx playwright install chromium
npm run test:e2e
\`\`\`

## Git hooks

The pre-commit hook runs lint-staged on staged files (lint-staged needs Node.js 22.22.1 or newer). Hooks are installed by \`prepare\` during install, which needs a git repository: after \`git init\`, run the install once more.

## License

MIT, see \`LICENSE\`.

## Progressive Web App

The production build is installable and works offline: \`vite-plugin-pwa\` writes the web manifest and a service worker that precaches the build, and updates it on the next visit after a deploy.

The icon is \`public/pwa-icon.svg\`. To also ship PNG icons (iOS home screen, older tools), generate them from it:

\`\`\`sh
npx @vite-pwa/assets-generator --preset minimal-2023 public/pwa-icon.svg
\`\`\`

## Deploy to Cloudflare

Run \`npm run deploy\`: it builds the site and uploads it to Cloudflare Workers. The first run opens a browser to log in.

To deploy from GitHub instead, connect the repository in the Cloudflare dashboard (Workers & Pages → Create → Import a repository).

## Docker

\`\`\`sh
docker build -t my-app .
docker run --rm -p 8080:80 my-app
\`\`\`

Then open http://localhost:8080.

## Deploy to Netlify

Push the project to GitHub and import it at https://app.netlify.com/start.
\`netlify.toml\` sets the build command and the folder to publish.

Or deploy from the terminal with \`npx netlify-cli deploy\`.

## Deploy to Vercel

Push the project to GitHub and import it at https://vercel.com/new. Vercel detects SolidJS and needs no build settings.

\`vercel.json\` sends every path to \`index.html\`, so client-side routes work on reload.

Or deploy from the terminal with \`npx vercel\`.

## Claude Code

\`CLAUDE.md\` (with \`AGENTS.md\`) describes the project, \`.claude/settings.json\` allows the project's scripts and formats edited files, and \`.mcp.json\` lists MCP servers for the stack (Claude Code asks before enabling them).

## SEO

Replace \`https://example.com\` in \`index.html\` and \`public/\` with your domain. This is a client-rendered app: crawlers that do not run JavaScript (social previews, most AI crawlers) only see the static tags in \`index.html\`. For per-page SEO use a meta-framework (Next.js, Nuxt, SvelteKit, Astro).

## Push to GitHub

Create an empty repository on GitHub, then:

\`\`\`bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/my-app.git
git push -u origin main
\`\`\`
",
  "e2e/app.e2e.js": "import { expect, test } from "@playwright/test";

test("the counter goes up", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto("/");
  await page.getByRole("button", { name: "+1" }).click();
  await expect(page.getByText("1", { exact: true })).toBeVisible();
});

test("the about page opens from the nav", async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto("/");
  await page.getByRole("link", { name: "About" }).click();
  await expect(page).toHaveURL(/about/);
  await expect(page.getByRole("heading", { name: "About" })).toBeVisible();
});
",
  "eslint.config.js": "import js from "@eslint/js";
import { defineConfig, globalIgnores } from "eslint/config";
import eslintConfigPrettier from "eslint-config-prettier/flat";
import solid from "eslint-plugin-solid/configs/recommended";
import globals from "globals";

export default defineConfig([
  globalIgnores(["dist"]),
  {
    files: ["**/*.{js,jsx}"],
    extends: [js.configs.recommended, solid],
    languageOptions: {
      globals: globals.browser,
    },
  },
  eslintConfigPrettier,
]);
",
  "index.html": "<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title>my-app</title>
    <meta name="description" content="my-app: a web app." />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://example.com/" />
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="my-app" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="my-app" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="my-app: a web app." />
    <meta property="og:url" content="https://example.com/" />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />
    <script type="application/ld+json">
      {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "WebSite",
        "name": "my-app",
        "url": "https://example.com/"
      }
    </script>
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#4f46e5" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/pwa-icon.svg" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <div id="root"></div>
    <script type="module" src="/src/index.jsx"></script>
  </body>
</html>
",
  "netlify.toml": "[build]
  command = "npm run build"
  publish = "dist"

# Client-side routes: serve index.html for paths that aren't files.
[[redirects]]
  from = "/*"
  to = "/index.html"
  status = 200
",
  "nginx.conf": "server {
  listen 80;
  server_name _;
  root /usr/share/nginx/html;
  index index.html;

  # Hashed file names change with every build, so they can be cached for good.
  location /assets/ {
    expires 1y;
    add_header Cache-Control "public, immutable";
  }

  location / {
    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
  }
}
",
