  "README.md": "# my-app

Stack: Next.js (App Router), React 19, TypeScript, ESLint, Turborepo.

## Getting started

\`\`\`bash
npm install
npm run dev
\`\`\`

## Scripts

- \`npm run build\`
- \`npm run typecheck\`
- \`npm run lint\`

## Monorepo

This is a Turborepo workspace: the app lives in \`apps/web\` and \`packages/\` is ready for shared code. Root scripts run the app's tasks through turbo, which caches their results.

## Push to GitHub

Create an empty repository on GitHub, then:

\`\`\`bash
git init
git add .
git commit -m "Initial commit"
git branch -M main
git remote add origin https://github.com/<your-username>/my-app.git
git push -u origin main
\`\`\`
